WEBVTT

01:02.729 --> 01:03.730
Stop!

01:06.024 --> 01:07.067
I...

01:07.901 --> 01:10.403
Can't you see I'm badly wounded?

01:40.100 --> 01:41.643
Still playing innocent?

01:41.726 --> 01:44.145
You murdered my brother!

01:46.439 --> 01:49.025
"Super robot detective," my ass!

01:49.109 --> 01:51.861
You're nothing but a murderous machine!

02:14.717 --> 02:16.344
You call this a safe house?

02:16.845 --> 02:18.388
It's just a log cabin!

02:19.055 --> 02:21.558
How can I protect myself
in a place like this?

02:21.641 --> 02:25.019
The inside is equipped
with a state-of-the-art security system.

02:25.603 --> 02:27.730
Hey! Where are you going?

02:27.814 --> 02:29.399
I'll be back in an hour.

02:29.482 --> 02:31.401
Get inside and don't leave,
no matter what.

02:31.484 --> 02:33.570
Your wife and son should be here soon.

02:34.320 --> 02:36.114
Hey, wait! You're abandoning your post?

02:36.906 --> 02:38.575
Your mission is to protect--

03:02.348 --> 03:04.559
<i>If you want to save your family,</i>

03:04.642 --> 03:06.728
kill Gesicht.

03:07.228 --> 03:11.608
Under the larch tree 200 steps north
of the safe house,

03:11.691 --> 03:13.526
there will be a weapon.

03:23.453 --> 03:24.287
Dad!

03:24.913 --> 03:25.747
Hans.

03:31.836 --> 03:33.421
Where's Gesicht?

03:35.423 --> 03:36.883
Don't mention his name.

03:37.383 --> 03:38.218
Dear.

03:39.552 --> 03:40.595
What's going on?

03:40.678 --> 03:43.223
I'm sorry to have worried you, Ilsa.

03:43.848 --> 03:46.309
Why must we go through all this?

03:48.895 --> 03:51.189
What in the world did you do?

04:03.368 --> 04:05.119
You're back, huh?

04:05.662 --> 04:07.622
He said you might be coming...

04:13.419 --> 04:15.505
Ah, there you are.

04:16.214 --> 04:18.258
So you finally remembered.

04:19.175 --> 04:21.261
How does it feel?

04:28.351 --> 04:29.811
Wow!

04:29.894 --> 04:33.189
The basement is like a fallout shelter!
And there's a gym too!

04:34.023 --> 04:35.483
Is that the whole truth?

04:38.319 --> 04:39.153
Yes.

04:39.737 --> 04:40.905
Unbelievable.

04:42.031 --> 04:43.866
To think you would go after Gesicht...

04:43.950 --> 04:46.411
I was hoping you'd understand.

04:46.494 --> 04:47.328
Well, I don't!

04:47.996 --> 04:52.083
Gesicht may have killed a human,
but we're talking about your brother!

04:57.046 --> 05:03.177
A goal! Hans is the champion!

05:04.262 --> 05:06.222
I'm sorry for what I'm about to say,

05:06.848 --> 05:10.268
but your brother deserved to die.

05:11.477 --> 05:15.440
He committed countless crimes,
and it's not just about the number.

05:16.149 --> 05:18.109
It sends chills down my spine.

05:18.192 --> 05:20.486
Just thinking about it makes me nauseous.

05:21.863 --> 05:24.824
Yes, he was a sick man.

05:24.907 --> 05:28.536
But even so, he didn't deserve
to be killed by a robot.

05:28.619 --> 05:31.456
You don't know that it was intentional.

05:31.998 --> 05:34.000
Robots can malfunction.

05:34.792 --> 05:36.502
No. It was his duty.

05:37.170 --> 05:39.714
Gesicht was faithfully following orders.

05:39.797 --> 05:42.216
He didn't do it
out of any particular emotion.

05:43.384 --> 05:44.344
Gesicht

05:45.011 --> 05:47.096
didn't kill your brother out of hatred.

05:50.433 --> 05:52.435
<i>You killed him out of hatred.</i>

05:53.519 --> 05:56.189
I knew it from the first moment I saw you.

05:56.814 --> 05:58.649
You and I are the same.

05:59.150 --> 06:03.237
Try as they might,
that memory will never be scrubbed away.

06:04.238 --> 06:07.992
The scar from that gaping wound
will always be there.

06:10.203 --> 06:11.037
Stop!

06:11.996 --> 06:13.081
I was wrong!

06:13.915 --> 06:15.124
I...

06:16.793 --> 06:19.670
Please spare me! Don't do it!

06:33.101 --> 06:36.270
Try and scratch that itch.

06:37.563 --> 06:42.902
Then you'll remember even more clearly
how true hatred feels.

06:49.951 --> 06:51.452
I must return to my post.

07:01.295 --> 07:07.385
<i>In the red corner, the WPKKR champion,</i>

07:07.468 --> 07:12.557
<i>the god of battle, Hercules!</i>

07:12.640 --> 07:15.017
Hercules!

08:00.271 --> 08:02.773
His opponent this time will be formidable.

08:03.399 --> 08:04.859
But that doesn't matter.

08:04.942 --> 08:08.863
The strong prevail
until someone stronger defeats them.

08:09.780 --> 08:11.657
That's all there is to it.

08:17.914 --> 08:19.749
The sea is getting rough.

08:21.918 --> 08:24.795
Listen, Gesicht
is investigating this case.

08:25.296 --> 08:28.299
Don't do anything reckless.
Work together to find a solution.

08:28.799 --> 08:30.760
Yes. We will.

08:41.395 --> 08:42.355
It's coming.

08:42.438 --> 08:44.023
You sense it too?

08:44.565 --> 08:46.817
Yes. Abnormal electromagnetic waves.

08:47.610 --> 08:48.569
Shall I help you?

08:50.196 --> 08:52.031
You are not equipped to help me here.

08:52.740 --> 08:55.743
True. I am not wired that way.

08:55.826 --> 08:58.663
And I am wired precisely for the task.

08:59.956 --> 09:02.208
I'm a machine made for battle.

09:03.167 --> 09:04.043
Leave quickly.

09:04.669 --> 09:08.172
A robot with no combat functions
will only slow me down.

09:10.424 --> 09:12.134
You're looking down on me again,

09:13.052 --> 09:15.555
just as you did
when I refused to fight in the war.

09:24.564 --> 09:27.441
Maybe you were right.

09:31.529 --> 09:35.533
Maybe you were right in refusing to fight.

09:37.076 --> 09:39.287
I am built to fight.

09:40.288 --> 09:43.749
But that war was no fight.

09:45.334 --> 09:46.168
<i>Back then,</i>

09:46.961 --> 09:49.088
<i>there was a robot who fought alongside me.</i>

09:50.339 --> 09:51.799
<i>As an airborne brigade elite,</i>

09:52.300 --> 09:55.553
<i>he helped lead us to success
on many missions through his actions.</i>

10:03.144 --> 10:06.230
<i>The last time I saw him,</i>

10:07.857 --> 10:10.526
<i>he kept washing his hands.</i>

10:11.861 --> 10:13.487
<i>Over and over again.</i>

10:14.238 --> 10:15.489
<i>Despite being a robot,</i>

10:16.490 --> 10:18.034
<i>he kept washing his hands.</i>

10:19.035 --> 10:21.412
Hey, what are you doing?

10:22.455 --> 10:23.581
It won't come off.

10:24.081 --> 10:25.166
What won't?

10:26.334 --> 10:27.668
It won't come off.

10:32.632 --> 10:35.676
The enemy coming our way is a ghost.

10:35.760 --> 10:36.594
A ghost?

10:37.219 --> 10:39.639
What I'm about to fight

10:41.265 --> 10:43.142
<i>are the ghosts of those who fell.</i>

10:46.437 --> 10:47.271
Go.

10:48.105 --> 10:49.398
You bear no guilt.

10:49.982 --> 10:51.525
You have no reason to be killed.

10:52.735 --> 10:54.320
But Atom was killed.

10:55.571 --> 10:58.991
He bore no guilt either,
so why was he killed?

11:03.371 --> 11:04.914
You know something.

11:04.997 --> 11:08.876
No, you learned something in that war.

11:08.959 --> 11:10.252
Just go.

11:14.090 --> 11:16.217
I'll be standing by at 3,000 meters.

11:17.009 --> 11:20.930
Suit yourself. You can collect the data
from my fight up there.

11:23.933 --> 11:27.853
I fight better when there's an audience,
even an audience of one.

11:29.063 --> 11:31.440
After all, I'm Hercules,
the god of battle.

11:51.669 --> 11:52.712
Brando...

11:53.546 --> 11:57.049
We fought many battles
that will go down in history.

11:57.550 --> 12:00.052
<i>They all ended in no contest.</i>

12:00.553 --> 12:03.472
<i>I wish we could have settled it, Brando.</i>

12:06.851 --> 12:09.228
We may not have been able
to settle our score,

12:09.895 --> 12:12.898
but I will settle it with this thing!

12:20.990 --> 12:23.826
However, this isn't a game.

12:27.580 --> 12:29.832
It's a fight to the death!

12:31.083 --> 12:33.627
They say the world
is made up of winners and losers,

12:33.711 --> 12:38.382
wise men and fools,
the living and the dead.

12:38.883 --> 12:43.095
But everyone is a loser, a fool, and dead.

12:43.763 --> 12:45.848
Everyone except for me.

12:58.611 --> 13:01.906
You won't fool me
with childish tricks like that!

13:15.461 --> 13:17.171
Die!

13:25.805 --> 13:29.683
I hereby declare
the 99th military tribunal in session.

13:30.184 --> 13:31.811
The defendant is to be sworn in.

13:35.105 --> 13:39.485
I order you to take the oath immediately,
defendant Darius XIV.

13:40.736 --> 13:41.987
Oath?

13:42.488 --> 13:45.199
God has no faith in the oaths of men.

13:45.282 --> 13:49.286
You have repeated the same response
99 times now.

13:49.370 --> 13:51.163
Take the oath immediately.

13:53.541 --> 13:55.835
Humans lie.

13:55.918 --> 13:58.504
God does not believe them.

13:58.587 --> 14:00.005
The defendant is out of order!

14:00.089 --> 14:03.676
In the eyes of God,
humanity is a failed creation.

14:04.176 --> 14:06.554
Humanity is in need of replacement.

14:07.137 --> 14:08.472
A new species.

14:09.098 --> 14:10.933
Robots are that species!

14:11.016 --> 14:12.893
Enough nonsense!

14:12.977 --> 14:15.688
Court is adjourned!
Remove the defendant from the courtroom!

14:15.771 --> 14:16.897
He's responsible!

14:16.981 --> 14:20.025
A new species?
You're the one who slaughtered them!

14:20.109 --> 14:22.820
You're full of contradictions!

14:22.903 --> 14:24.947
- Order in the court!
- That's right!

14:25.030 --> 14:26.866
There are no contradictions.

14:27.700 --> 14:29.493
That was no slaughter.

14:30.160 --> 14:31.662
It was an evolutionary stage.

14:31.745 --> 14:34.373
Hold Darius in contempt of court!

14:34.456 --> 14:35.875
Darius must be sentenced!

14:35.958 --> 14:37.751
Death to Darius!

14:39.628 --> 14:41.797
I'm from a human rights organization.

14:41.881 --> 14:43.799
If there's anything we can do to help you...

14:46.051 --> 14:47.887
Bring me crayons.

14:54.101 --> 14:55.102
Hercules...

14:59.982 --> 15:02.484
These parts are his...

15:03.319 --> 15:04.862
No, some belong to the enemy!

15:05.487 --> 15:06.822
Did they destroy each other?

15:12.077 --> 15:14.705
<i>That's the body Hercules uses
for daily life.</i>

15:20.461 --> 15:22.338
What is going on?

15:22.838 --> 15:24.965
The parts are scattered all over the sea--

15:26.216 --> 15:28.218
The abnormal electromagnetic waves are--

15:37.144 --> 15:38.020
That's...

15:38.103 --> 15:41.982
If I can break off this horn,

15:42.524 --> 15:43.651
then surely you will...

15:46.862 --> 15:48.948
If I help him now,
we can defeat the enemy!

16:06.423 --> 16:09.301
Hey, what are you doing?

16:10.386 --> 16:11.553
It won't come off.

16:12.346 --> 16:13.305
What won't?

16:16.392 --> 16:17.726
It won't come off.

16:21.355 --> 16:23.399
What are these images?

16:24.274 --> 16:26.068
I can't move my body!

16:27.194 --> 16:29.071
So that's

16:29.989 --> 16:31.031
who you are!

16:50.342 --> 16:52.886
It's way past lights out.

16:53.470 --> 16:54.388
What are you doing?

16:56.807 --> 16:59.435
When the flood returns,

17:00.019 --> 17:01.770
the ones who board the ark,

17:02.438 --> 17:04.398
the ones chosen by God...

17:04.481 --> 17:05.357
Hey!

17:05.441 --> 17:09.319
Humans or robots, which will it be?

17:09.403 --> 17:10.571
Open up.

17:11.530 --> 17:13.073
The only one who will survive...

17:14.616 --> 17:15.617
What the...

17:17.327 --> 17:18.746
...is Pluto.

17:21.165 --> 17:22.332
Hercules!

17:41.894 --> 17:42.853
<i>Where</i>

17:44.313 --> 17:45.147
<i>am I?</i>

17:46.774 --> 17:47.608
<i>I'm</i>

17:48.734 --> 17:49.818
<i>running away.</i>

17:51.195 --> 17:52.196
<i>From what?</i>

18:06.418 --> 18:07.961
Hercules is dead.

18:09.880 --> 18:11.090
I must let him know.

18:12.549 --> 18:13.550
I must!

18:14.259 --> 18:16.637
Only he has the authority
to arrest the enemy.

18:17.638 --> 18:18.514
Gesicht.

18:21.350 --> 18:22.267
Gesicht?

18:22.851 --> 18:24.061
Gesicht?

18:24.812 --> 18:26.271
The channel's been cut off!

18:27.022 --> 18:27.898
<i>Gesicht!</i>

18:28.649 --> 18:29.983
<i>Gesicht, please respond!</i>

18:30.484 --> 18:31.485
<i>Gesicht!</i>

18:31.568 --> 18:34.947
<i>Did you have the same look
in your eyes back then?</i>

18:35.030 --> 18:38.075
You're the one who killed my brother!

18:39.660 --> 18:41.829
Right this way, please.

18:44.331 --> 18:47.292
Could you confirm that this is your child?

18:55.050 --> 18:56.844
Gesicht, I can take it from here.

18:57.386 --> 18:58.470
Check the other room.

19:11.191 --> 19:13.652
There's no mistake. This is our child.

19:22.953 --> 19:26.331
Humans cry like that
in these situations, don't they?

19:29.459 --> 19:31.044
I understand somewhat.

19:31.795 --> 19:33.463
Yes.

19:36.216 --> 19:40.846
We applied as soon as
the Robot Adoption System was launched.

19:41.722 --> 19:44.641
It took four years
until this child came to us.

19:46.018 --> 19:50.105
There were many couples
on the waiting list, you know?

19:50.814 --> 19:53.901
I was so happy
when I met this child for the first time.

19:54.568 --> 19:55.402
Yes.

19:56.695 --> 20:00.282
We're finally living in an age
when robots can have families.

20:00.908 --> 20:04.536
We thought we could live as a family.

20:09.791 --> 20:13.212
I'm Gesicht. I'll be joining
the investigation from today on.

20:13.295 --> 20:14.171
Nice to meet you.

20:14.254 --> 20:17.424
Is it a good idea
to have a robot on this case?

20:17.925 --> 20:19.426
I'm just following orders.

20:19.927 --> 20:23.931
Robot children were kidnapped
and torn to pieces.

20:24.556 --> 20:27.726
The crimes may have been committed
by someone with anti-robot beliefs.

20:27.809 --> 20:30.896
Your involvement could be considered
a conflict of interest.

20:30.979 --> 20:34.608
Yes, and that's why I will
only investigate other possibilities.

20:40.030 --> 20:41.323
What about the surveillance?

20:43.116 --> 20:46.745
Like the others, the kidnapping took place
after the B-Com Eye 3 was destroyed.

20:47.371 --> 20:50.207
In all, there have been
23 kidnapping cases like this one.

20:50.290 --> 20:54.419
Every time, the perpetrator kidnapped
the kid after destroying the system.

20:55.254 --> 20:58.465
There are 304 places
where B-Com Eye 3 systems were installed.

20:58.548 --> 21:02.678
All known robot haters, radicals,
and ex-convicts in the area

21:02.761 --> 21:05.180
were recorded elsewhere
at the time of the crime.

21:05.264 --> 21:09.226
Which means all of our suspects
have an alibi.

21:12.479 --> 21:14.106
<i>What is the meaning of this?</i>

21:14.773 --> 21:18.235
Why did you tell the media
that I joined the investigation?

21:18.318 --> 21:19.987
It's a diversionary tactic.

21:22.364 --> 21:28.161
We'll show the public
how committed we are to solving the case.

21:28.829 --> 21:29.830
More importantly,

21:29.913 --> 21:34.001
your involvement might prevent
the next crime from happening.

21:35.836 --> 21:39.256
We've narrowed the list of robot haters
to those not seen on surveillance

21:39.339 --> 21:41.967
in the Euro Federation
at the time of the crime.

21:42.050 --> 21:43.510
There are seven of them.

21:43.593 --> 21:46.013
They're all under surveillance right now.

21:46.096 --> 21:48.348
What is the failure rate
of B-Com Eye 3 systems?

21:48.432 --> 21:49.266
Huh?

21:50.017 --> 21:54.604
Can you compare the failure rates
before and after the incidents?

21:54.688 --> 21:57.774
Oh, the manufacturer has that data.

21:57.858 --> 22:02.154
The system itself is top-notch,
but it is prone to failures.

22:02.696 --> 22:04.823
The failure rate over the last three years

22:05.615 --> 22:07.492
is 3.26%.

22:07.576 --> 22:10.495
And after the incidents...

22:11.371 --> 22:12.205
Huh?

22:12.289 --> 22:14.666
It's 3.25%.

22:14.750 --> 22:18.045
Though the crimes were committed
after the suspect destroyed the system,

22:18.128 --> 22:19.880
the failure rate isn't affected.

22:22.424 --> 22:25.594
<i>We have a report
of a kidnapping in Ward W-25!</i>

22:25.677 --> 22:27.346
<i>The victim is a robot child!</i>

22:27.971 --> 22:30.098
Gesicht, head to the scene.

22:30.640 --> 22:31.475
Yes, sir.

22:33.101 --> 22:35.812
Helena? Sorry.
I'm responding to an emergency.

22:37.773 --> 22:39.024
What?

22:41.651 --> 22:42.486
What's wrong?

22:45.280 --> 22:46.782
Hey, where are you going?

22:47.282 --> 22:49.701
- Henry!
- I'm coming!

22:49.785 --> 22:52.412
Find the causes
of the B-Com Eye 3 failures.

22:52.496 --> 22:53.330
What?

22:53.413 --> 22:55.665
I can't access the data in this case.

22:55.749 --> 22:57.876
I need your help.

22:57.959 --> 23:00.045
But if we don't hurry to the scene--

23:00.128 --> 23:01.421
Just do it now!

23:02.005 --> 23:02.839
Gesicht?

23:03.340 --> 23:04.925
You don't sound like yourself.

23:08.637 --> 23:12.349
These are the causes of all failures
occurring in the last three months.

23:12.432 --> 23:17.104
Three outages due to lightning strikes
and 38 problems with control chips.

23:17.187 --> 23:19.731
Can you compare that
to data from the last three years?

23:19.815 --> 23:20.649
Okay.

23:21.983 --> 23:23.819
The ratio is pretty much the same.

23:24.319 --> 23:27.364
The perpetrator
didn't destroy the systems.

23:27.447 --> 23:28.323
What?

23:28.824 --> 23:32.911
But it's possible to emit electromagnetic
waves that are identical to lightning...

23:34.579 --> 23:38.792
There is one case where the system
was clearly destroyed by human means.

23:38.875 --> 23:40.252
It happened yesterday?

23:40.335 --> 23:43.213
But there were no kidnappings yesterday.

23:43.713 --> 23:45.590
Show the list of maintenance contractors.

23:46.842 --> 23:50.095
Bring up the maintenance contractors
in the kidnappings' vicinity!

23:52.097 --> 23:54.349
It didn't start with the system's failure.

23:54.433 --> 23:56.017
It started with its repair!

23:57.394 --> 24:00.230
There's only one person responsible
for repairing the system

24:00.313 --> 24:01.857
at the kidnapping site!

24:12.033 --> 24:13.702
Hey, Gesicht?

24:13.785 --> 24:16.455
<i>Gesicht! Do you copy, Gesicht?</i>

24:16.538 --> 24:18.498
<i>Gesicht isn't responding!</i>

24:18.582 --> 24:20.417
<i>It's no use.
The comm channel has been shut off.</i>

24:20.500 --> 24:24.629
<i>Respond, Gesicht!
This is insubordination! Gesicht!</i>

24:24.713 --> 24:26.089
Stop!

24:26.756 --> 24:28.300
Please don't!

24:33.597 --> 24:35.974
Don't shoot me!

24:54.868 --> 24:55.702
No, I can't.

24:58.538 --> 25:01.333
I can't run away from this.

25:10.926 --> 25:11.760
Damn it!

25:12.719 --> 25:14.513
There will be a weapon.

25:16.306 --> 25:19.017
Where the hell is this so-called weapon?

25:19.100 --> 25:20.143
Mr. Haas!

25:21.311 --> 25:23.730
Oh, I'm Meyer from Europol.

25:24.231 --> 25:26.066
What are you doing there?

25:26.650 --> 25:29.903
You want me to go back
to the safe house, right? I know.

25:30.403 --> 25:31.905
No, that's not it.

25:31.988 --> 25:37.494
You stopped at a rest area by the forest
before you got here, didn't you?

25:38.328 --> 25:39.538
What about it?

25:39.621 --> 25:43.208
There was a suspicious man
on the security camera footage from there.

25:43.291 --> 25:44.709
We looked into him,

25:44.793 --> 25:47.712
and it seems he's a member
of the organization that's after you.

25:48.255 --> 25:50.715
They know your movements.

25:51.216 --> 25:53.385
We must transfer you
to another location now.

25:53.468 --> 25:54.844
Oh, I see.

25:54.928 --> 25:56.388
Inspector Meyer!

25:57.973 --> 25:59.307
Gesicht is back.

25:59.933 --> 26:01.059
Hey, Gesicht!

26:01.643 --> 26:04.062
You're not to leave your post
without permission!

26:04.729 --> 26:06.106
I'm sorry, sir.

26:06.189 --> 26:09.276
It's unthinkable for a robot
to do something like this.

26:09.359 --> 26:11.278
I'll have to file a report later.

26:11.361 --> 26:13.238
But for now, Mr. Haas's protection--

26:13.321 --> 26:16.032
I heard the situation.
I will move him right away.

26:18.410 --> 26:19.744
Let's go, Mr. Haas.

26:20.620 --> 26:22.080
Abandoning your mission, huh?

26:23.206 --> 26:24.749
Just like back then.

26:24.833 --> 26:27.252
What you did to my brother
was not your mission.

26:29.254 --> 26:33.008
My mission right now is to protect you.

26:45.937 --> 26:48.982
Say, which direction
are the bad guys coming from?

26:49.065 --> 26:50.859
Stop talking nonsense and sit down!

26:51.443 --> 26:54.112
But we'll be okay
no matter where they come from, right?

26:54.195 --> 26:55.655
Because Gesicht is here!

26:56.156 --> 26:58.700
The other inspector's car behind us
is guarding the rear.

26:59.200 --> 27:00.869
You don't need to worry, Hans.

27:00.952 --> 27:03.455
What will you do if the bad guys show up?

27:03.538 --> 27:06.750
- Does your arm transform into a gun?
- Hans!

27:06.833 --> 27:11.963
But I learned in school
that robots can't shoot people.

27:12.047 --> 27:14.215
How are you going to do them in?

27:14.799 --> 27:16.760
He'll shoot them if it comes to that.

27:16.843 --> 27:17.677
Right?

27:18.303 --> 27:19.679
That's enough, dear.

27:20.722 --> 27:22.098
What is it?

27:22.599 --> 27:24.100
The car behind us...

27:25.894 --> 27:28.813
Wait, I don't see the inspector's car!

27:30.690 --> 27:31.941
I've lost communication.

27:32.442 --> 27:33.276
They're coming!

27:36.571 --> 27:37.697
Someone's after us?

27:38.281 --> 27:40.700
I'm going to speed up.
Fasten your seat belts!

27:47.374 --> 27:49.292
They're speeding up--

27:54.673 --> 27:57.175
The police car disappeared in an instant.

27:57.258 --> 27:59.302
The weapon they're using could be...

27:59.386 --> 28:00.804
A compact cluster cannon.

28:02.639 --> 28:03.473
Most likely,

28:04.432 --> 28:06.476
it's the same model I had acquired

28:07.018 --> 28:08.812
since it's strong enough to kill you.

28:13.858 --> 28:16.027
Help us, please!

28:17.570 --> 28:19.280
At least my wife and my son.

28:20.198 --> 28:21.032
Please.

28:23.702 --> 28:25.870
The robot at the rest area told me

28:26.830 --> 28:28.915
that if I wanted to save my family,

28:30.041 --> 28:30.917
I'd have to

28:32.085 --> 28:33.211
kill you.

28:34.045 --> 28:35.171
But from the start,

28:35.255 --> 28:38.425
they were planning
to dispose of all of us,

28:39.342 --> 28:42.262
so I couldn't expose the truth
about the anti-robot cult.

28:44.013 --> 28:45.432
I hate you.

28:46.057 --> 28:47.559
You killed my brother.

28:48.351 --> 28:49.394
That's why

28:50.145 --> 28:51.771
I tried to kill you.

28:53.189 --> 28:54.315
This hatred,

28:54.941 --> 28:57.777
you know it too, even if you are a robot.

28:59.904 --> 29:03.199
Without hatred,
you could never kill someone like that.

29:04.743 --> 29:08.371
But that's between you,
me, and my brother!

29:08.872 --> 29:11.166
My family has nothing to do with this!

29:12.041 --> 29:12.876
Please...

29:13.460 --> 29:15.462
Please save my wife and my son!

29:16.629 --> 29:19.090
Mr. Haas, grab the lever to your right.

29:19.174 --> 29:21.009
- What?
- Grab the lever to your right!

29:26.514 --> 29:27.557
Hans! Mrs. Haas!

29:32.896 --> 29:34.773
Hans! Ilsa!

29:40.487 --> 29:41.696
Hans! Ilsa!

29:42.822 --> 29:43.782
Hans!

29:43.865 --> 29:44.824
Ilsa!

29:51.915 --> 29:55.126
A regular gun is enough for you.

29:55.752 --> 29:57.378
But the leader told me

29:58.588 --> 30:01.007
to make this all look like
it was your doing,

30:01.508 --> 30:05.220
and that you died in the explosion
from the cluster cannon.

30:07.514 --> 30:09.140
No hard feelings.

30:09.974 --> 30:11.351
Drop your weapon!

30:11.434 --> 30:13.561
Ah, the robot detective.

30:13.645 --> 30:16.064
Aren't you forbidden
from firing your right arm?

30:16.147 --> 30:17.565
I'm a human, you see?

30:19.984 --> 30:22.487
You're not allowed to kill humans, right?

30:23.780 --> 30:26.991
Come any closer,
and I'll fire this bad boy.

30:28.493 --> 30:30.829
Mr. Haas, walk toward me slowly.

30:34.082 --> 30:35.792
Step slowly behind me.

30:40.171 --> 30:41.422
Suits me just fine.

30:41.923 --> 30:46.052
This cluster cannon can easily blast
the two of you into pieces,

30:46.135 --> 30:49.055
even if you're made of Zeronium.

30:49.138 --> 30:52.016
Two birds with one stone.

30:52.100 --> 30:53.142
Get behind me!

31:20.378 --> 31:23.798
My left arm shoots sleeping gas.

31:24.799 --> 31:27.635
You can surrender quietly,
and I'll read you your rights,

31:28.219 --> 31:30.346
or you can be knocked out by the gas.

31:31.639 --> 31:32.640
Which will it be?

31:33.516 --> 31:34.392
Say it.

31:39.188 --> 31:40.023
Gesicht.

31:41.441 --> 31:43.401
My brother was the worst of the worst.

31:45.486 --> 31:46.571
And yet,

31:47.530 --> 31:49.365
you used your own body to shield me,

31:50.575 --> 31:52.076
the man who tried to kill you.

31:53.494 --> 31:54.537
It was my duty.

31:55.121 --> 31:55.955
Gesicht...

31:57.206 --> 31:59.709
Mr. Haas, there's something
I want to ask you.

32:01.210 --> 32:03.463
Does the hatred you humans feel
ever disappear?

32:04.213 --> 32:05.423
Or does it never go away,

32:05.924 --> 32:08.384
no matter how many times
you try to erase it?

32:12.221 --> 32:14.349
What I was most afraid of...

32:17.852 --> 32:19.562
is myself,

32:20.605 --> 32:22.315
now that I've learned how to hate.

32:32.200 --> 32:36.537
She's been keeping to herself
on the schoolyard these days.

32:38.289 --> 32:42.251
She used to be so cheerful,
but she doesn't talk much anymore,

32:43.086 --> 32:44.587
not since the incident.

32:46.339 --> 32:49.008
I guess it proves
how advanced she is as a robot.

32:49.092 --> 32:51.678
Who knew a robot could go through
a personality change...

32:51.761 --> 32:53.054
Of course she could!

32:54.430 --> 32:58.726
Robots feel sorrow and shed tears,
just like humans do.

32:58.810 --> 33:00.436
Principal...

33:01.396 --> 33:04.148
There are no high or low specs
when it comes to the heart.

33:04.232 --> 33:06.025
You're right, sir.

33:06.943 --> 33:11.823
Even an old robot model like me
feels sorrow.

33:11.906 --> 33:13.992
Mr. Sakamoto...

33:16.703 --> 33:17.787
But the question is,

33:17.870 --> 33:20.665
what can we do as educators
in a situation like this?

33:21.290 --> 33:24.210
How can we save her from her sorrow?

33:27.088 --> 33:30.508
Uran, you aren't the only one

33:31.634 --> 33:33.261
who grieves Atom's loss.

33:50.528 --> 33:51.821
I feel something.

33:56.034 --> 33:59.287
Something out there
is feeling sadder than I am.

34:18.389 --> 34:20.683
Was it you who was feeling so sad?

34:21.267 --> 34:22.393
Where's your mommy?

34:23.978 --> 34:24.854
No.

34:25.855 --> 34:27.273
It's coming from over there.

34:39.827 --> 34:40.661
Is it you?

34:44.248 --> 34:46.751
Are you the one who is feeling sad?

34:46.834 --> 34:48.461
Leave me alone.

34:52.340 --> 34:55.384
There's an electromagnetic net below,
so there's no use jumping.

34:55.468 --> 34:56.302
Then...

34:57.553 --> 34:59.722
then what am I supposed to do?

35:00.223 --> 35:02.642
I get bullied day in and day out.

35:03.184 --> 35:05.436
They threaten me for money!

35:05.520 --> 35:07.438
They call me dirty and stinky!

35:10.983 --> 35:13.361
What am I supposed to do?

35:17.031 --> 35:19.492
I'd be better off dead.

35:23.746 --> 35:24.747
I don't understand.

35:25.748 --> 35:26.582
Huh?

35:27.625 --> 35:30.253
I don't understand what it feels like
to want to die

35:30.753 --> 35:32.255
because I'm a robot.

35:32.338 --> 35:35.842
How could a robot possibly understand?

35:36.509 --> 35:39.053
I'm not programmed that way.

35:40.263 --> 35:42.098
Just leave me alone already.

35:43.391 --> 35:44.767
And that's why my brother

35:46.018 --> 35:48.104
had no feeling of wanting to die.

35:49.188 --> 35:50.565
Yet, he was killed.

35:52.441 --> 35:55.111
Right now, I'm really sad.

35:56.404 --> 35:58.197
If I were human,

35:58.781 --> 36:01.450
would I want to die like you?

36:05.496 --> 36:10.084
This kitten was sad too,
but it didn't want to die.

36:10.835 --> 36:14.839
All it thinks about is how it wants milk
and how hungry it is.

36:17.383 --> 36:18.759
Was that cat abandoned?

36:32.398 --> 36:34.108
It's pretty cute.

36:34.650 --> 36:37.904
But we've got to feed it soon.
It's shaking.

36:38.946 --> 36:40.907
Can you get some milk for the cat?

36:40.990 --> 36:41.824
What?

36:41.908 --> 36:44.202
There's someone even sadder over there!

36:46.120 --> 36:46.954
Hey!

36:57.840 --> 36:59.800
Is this what you're looking for?

37:00.801 --> 37:01.928
Oh!

37:02.553 --> 37:05.181
Yes, this is my wallet.

37:06.557 --> 37:11.395
I put my pension card in here
so I could buy a gift for my grandchild.

37:12.188 --> 37:14.023
Thank you.

37:14.565 --> 37:15.566
I'm truly grate...

37:24.659 --> 37:25.576
It's here.

37:26.786 --> 37:29.288
I can sense
such immense sadness from here.

37:41.634 --> 37:42.635
This is the spot.

37:44.303 --> 37:46.555
The person I sensed was just here.

37:47.765 --> 37:49.058
Incredible sadness...

37:50.601 --> 37:54.063
As if they experienced
the same person dying twice.

37:58.067 --> 38:01.070
"Tobio... Tenma."

38:08.411 --> 38:10.162
Oh, Minister Ochanomizu.

38:10.246 --> 38:12.248
The Chief Cabinet Secretary
called many times...

38:12.331 --> 38:13.165
Let them wait.

38:13.249 --> 38:14.417
But, sir...

38:15.167 --> 38:18.629
Tell them I have no interest
in discussing a state funeral for Atom.

38:19.380 --> 38:21.007
I'm not giving up yet.

38:22.049 --> 38:24.760
More importantly,
have you heard back from him yet?

38:24.844 --> 38:25.678
"Him"?

38:26.345 --> 38:27.763
I told you! The former minis--

38:27.847 --> 38:29.598
You can't enter without permission!

38:30.141 --> 38:32.226
Please make an appointment.

38:32.310 --> 38:34.729
Otherwise, the security system
cannot verify you.

38:34.812 --> 38:36.814
There will be no problem with security.

38:36.897 --> 38:38.190
But, like I said...

38:38.858 --> 38:41.402
I am the former head
of the Ministry of Science.

38:41.485 --> 38:42.903
- What?
- Dr. Tenma!

38:42.987 --> 38:45.614
You came! I've been waiting for you!

38:48.576 --> 38:50.661
I knew you'd come.

38:51.162 --> 38:53.873
You're the only one
who can save Atom in his current state.

38:53.956 --> 38:56.334
Only you, the one who brought Atom
into the world.

38:56.417 --> 38:58.044
It's impossible. He can't be saved.

38:59.628 --> 39:01.005
I've come to say goodbye.

39:01.672 --> 39:03.215
Atom is dead.

39:26.364 --> 39:27.281
Tobio is

39:27.990 --> 39:29.116
dead.

39:42.296 --> 39:45.132
Tobio, what did you do today?

39:45.216 --> 39:46.384
Today?

39:46.467 --> 39:51.055
Today, I studied in the morning
and cleaned up my room in the afternoon.

39:51.138 --> 39:54.266
I found an insect encyclopedia
at the back of my bookcase.

39:54.350 --> 39:57.937
It was so interesting
that I forgot all about cleaning.

39:58.521 --> 40:00.856
There's a pretty butterfly
called a zephyrus.

40:00.940 --> 40:03.192
I'd love to see one in real life.

40:06.362 --> 40:07.196
Tobio.

40:10.408 --> 40:12.535
Do you think this dish is tasty?

40:12.618 --> 40:14.995
Yes, it's really tasty!

40:16.789 --> 40:17.957
I see.

40:45.985 --> 40:47.736
Minister! Minister Ochanomizu!

40:48.821 --> 40:50.114
It's Dr. Tenma!

40:50.781 --> 40:54.743
He's repairing Atom!
He's trying to revive him!

40:55.327 --> 40:57.913
It's incredible.
I've never seen anything like it!

40:57.997 --> 41:02.835
He's connected RS-889 while simultaneously
controlling the motherboard!

41:02.918 --> 41:04.795
And he's randomly replacing motion data.

41:05.713 --> 41:11.635
<i>Outputting data to H2K-4380.
Releasing shield on Troy 647K.</i>

41:11.719 --> 41:14.263
<i>Updating TNT module.</i>

41:14.346 --> 41:16.474
<i>BQ lines on auto control.</i>

41:28.319 --> 41:31.405
Are we witnessing
the technique of a true genius?

41:32.114 --> 41:34.742
You said you came to say goodbye.

41:36.076 --> 41:38.787
I knew you would do this.

41:40.414 --> 41:41.665
Dr. Tenma...

41:52.968 --> 41:57.515
After working nonstop for 18 hours,
you should get some rest.

41:59.975 --> 42:01.519
I'll leave your tea here.

42:06.482 --> 42:08.776
So, what do you think about
Atom's prognosis?

42:08.859 --> 42:12.196
The head of the Ministry of Science,
Professor Ochanomizu,

42:12.279 --> 42:14.573
poured everything he had into him.

42:15.866 --> 42:17.368
Your operations were brilliant.

42:17.451 --> 42:19.578
Spare me the jokes.

42:21.539 --> 42:23.582
No abnormalities
in his artificial hippocampus

42:23.666 --> 42:25.876
nor his artificial right and left brains.

42:25.960 --> 42:30.047
The receptor adjustment,
synaptic cleft, everything checks out.

42:30.923 --> 42:34.009
Your repair work was perfect.

42:34.093 --> 42:36.470
Then why won't Atom wake up?

42:41.100 --> 42:45.646
Why did Atom have to meet such a fate?

42:48.691 --> 42:52.611
This case involves the destruction
of all the world's most advanced robots.

42:53.112 --> 42:54.071
You know this, yes?

42:55.781 --> 43:02.580
And the former members of the Bora Inquiry
Commission are being killed one by one.

43:06.792 --> 43:07.876
Dr. Tenma,

43:09.295 --> 43:11.964
do you know of a person named Goji?

43:13.841 --> 43:15.175
I do not.

43:15.259 --> 43:17.136
That can't be true!

43:17.219 --> 43:21.140
I'm talking about Dr. Goji, who built
the robot army of the Kingdom of Persia!

43:21.223 --> 43:26.270
The robot army that was only possible
because the AI you developed

43:26.353 --> 43:29.189
was leaked to them. Am I wrong?

43:33.110 --> 43:34.528
I have no idea.

43:35.613 --> 43:36.989
My artificial intelligence

43:37.072 --> 43:39.491
shouldn't be wasted
on the likes of a robot army.

43:41.452 --> 43:44.580
A robot with my artificial intelligence

43:45.247 --> 43:48.292
would be more noble and more complete.

43:50.419 --> 43:51.545
Wanna know something?

43:52.046 --> 43:55.507
I once created a perfect robot.

43:58.135 --> 44:00.304
It was commissioned
by a certain individual.

44:01.055 --> 44:04.516
I told them it would be extremely costly,
but they insisted.

44:05.893 --> 44:10.356
The artificial intelligence of the world's
most advanced robots, including Atom.

44:10.856 --> 44:15.486
Their programming is extremely complex,
but there are limitations.

44:16.987 --> 44:20.115
So, what do you think I did?

44:23.285 --> 44:25.996
I analyzed and programmed
9.9 billion personalities,

44:26.080 --> 44:30.334
the same number as the world's population.

44:33.420 --> 44:34.546
In other words,

44:34.630 --> 44:39.593
I put every single option and possibility
into that artificial intelligence.

44:39.677 --> 44:41.428
A brilliant idea, no?

44:41.929 --> 44:44.264
Such a robot
could potentially become anything.

44:44.765 --> 44:48.686
A grump, a coward,
a crybaby, a hard worker,

44:48.769 --> 44:52.272
a scholar, a hero, or a genius?

44:52.356 --> 44:54.066
Perhaps a murderer?

44:56.151 --> 44:59.029
What do you think happened to that robot?

45:05.703 --> 45:07.621
<i>It never woke up.</i>

45:07.705 --> 45:11.792
<i>No, I should probably say
that it refused to wake up.</i>

45:13.627 --> 45:15.212
It was too complicated.

45:15.295 --> 45:20.551
It would take an eternity
to simulate 9.9 billion personalities.

45:21.510 --> 45:24.596
But I knew how to wake it up.

45:25.222 --> 45:29.184
All I had to do was to steer the chaos
of the 9.9 billion in one direction.

45:30.310 --> 45:31.395
How?

45:32.187 --> 45:33.814
By destroying the balance.

45:34.314 --> 45:36.900
Anger, sorrow, hatred...

45:37.443 --> 45:40.112
By infusing unbalanced emotions.

45:40.696 --> 45:43.574
Unbalanced emotions?

45:44.158 --> 45:49.538
Yes. Imbalance is the program
that simplifies chaos.

45:49.621 --> 45:51.790
But if you did something like that...

45:56.128 --> 45:59.047
Where is that robot now?

45:59.840 --> 46:01.008
Who knows.

46:01.091 --> 46:05.554
The owner must have it hidden away,
still asleep.

46:09.016 --> 46:09.933
Don't tell me...

46:10.934 --> 46:15.397
Are you saying that Atom is
in the same state right now, Dr. Tenma?

46:15.939 --> 46:19.902
That he has sensed something inconceivable
and is simulating the response endlessly?

46:20.402 --> 46:25.073
Atom won't wake up for the same reason
your perfect robot didn't wake up?

46:28.619 --> 46:30.412
Are you suggesting

46:30.496 --> 46:33.332
that we infuse Atom
with unbalanced emotions to wake him?

46:34.374 --> 46:35.626
If we did that,

46:36.460 --> 46:40.839
Atom could be reborn
as something horribly different!

46:42.883 --> 46:44.051
Yes.

46:44.968 --> 46:47.638
He might come back a monster.

46:52.476 --> 46:53.393
I see.

46:54.019 --> 46:55.270
You think it's tasty?

46:55.354 --> 46:56.313
Yes!

46:58.023 --> 46:58.857
Tobio.

46:59.358 --> 47:00.734
Yes, Dad?

47:01.527 --> 47:04.905
The real Tobio died in a traffic accident.

47:08.700 --> 47:10.327
But I'm here now.

47:10.410 --> 47:14.706
Tobio was terrible at cleaning,
and his room was always a mess.

47:15.249 --> 47:17.251
Okay, from tomorrow,
I won't clean as much--

47:17.334 --> 47:19.878
Tobio hated studying.

47:22.673 --> 47:23.590
Then I won't study--

47:23.674 --> 47:25.592
Tobio stuffed
the encyclopedia I bought him

47:25.676 --> 47:28.345
in the back of the bookshelf
without looking at it.

47:30.514 --> 47:31.348
Tobio

47:32.057 --> 47:34.768
hated this dish.

47:39.773 --> 47:42.568
Do you like me?

47:42.651 --> 47:45.070
Yes, I love you, Dad.

47:45.863 --> 47:49.074
I was so hard on Tobio,
scolding him all the time.

47:50.993 --> 47:53.829
Because of that, I'm sure that Tobio...

48:00.377 --> 48:02.546
hated me.

48:07.843 --> 48:08.844
<i>Gesicht?</i>

48:10.262 --> 48:11.305
<i>Do you read me?</i>

48:12.014 --> 48:12.931
<i>Gesicht!</i>

48:14.433 --> 48:16.810
<i>Hoffman here. Please respond, Gesicht!</i>

48:17.311 --> 48:19.271
<i>You're still in the middle of an overhaul.</i>

48:19.354 --> 48:21.440
<i>It's too dangerous
for you to return to work!</i>

48:22.065 --> 48:25.777
<i>There is still shrapnel
from the cluster cannon in your body!</i>

48:26.570 --> 48:27.404
<i>Gesicht?</i>

48:28.030 --> 48:29.448
<i>Please respond, Gesicht!</i>

48:30.574 --> 48:32.242
<i>Gesicht, this is Epsilon.</i>

48:32.743 --> 48:33.952
<i>It's urgent. I need to--</i>

48:35.579 --> 48:36.413
<i>...right away--</i>

49:02.731 --> 49:06.360
I have an appointment.
I am Gesicht from Europol.

49:09.363 --> 49:11.823
Verified. Please enter.

49:16.411 --> 49:18.538
<i>Please wait in B-325.</i>

49:27.172 --> 49:28.382
Welcome.

49:28.966 --> 49:32.094
I'm Colonel Armstrong
of the United States of Thracia Army.

49:33.053 --> 49:34.888
Gesicht of Europol.

49:34.972 --> 49:37.849
Our nation did not join
the International Criminal Law Treaty.

49:37.933 --> 49:42.813
Your request has been granted
by a special directive from the president.

49:43.647 --> 49:47.693
Time is limited, so I ask that you
complete your business here quickly.

49:48.193 --> 49:49.486
- Begin.
- Yes, sir.

49:50.904 --> 49:52.823
Begin right here?

49:52.906 --> 49:54.366
Yes. Is there a problem?

49:55.117 --> 49:55.951
Well, no...

49:56.034 --> 49:58.078
What are you doing? Hurry it up.

49:58.161 --> 49:58.996
Yes, sir.

50:00.205 --> 50:02.457
This is
a state-of-the-art prison facility,

50:02.541 --> 50:04.710
but as you can see,
our robots are outdated.

50:05.419 --> 50:08.130
Our country is
on the cutting edge of technology,

50:08.213 --> 50:11.174
but as you may know,
we're far behind in the robot industry.

50:11.758 --> 50:14.344
If we had excellent robots like you,

50:14.428 --> 50:16.847
the restoration of Persia
could have gone faster.

50:17.431 --> 50:19.558
But from a human rights perspective,

50:19.641 --> 50:22.060
we do not produce
robots of mass destruction.

50:24.187 --> 50:25.272
The link is up.

50:26.815 --> 50:28.150
Make it short, please.

50:35.365 --> 50:37.909
You really expect me
to interview him like this?

50:38.410 --> 50:40.037
Yes. Is there a problem?

50:43.248 --> 50:45.500
You're Darius XIV, correct?

50:47.794 --> 50:48.712
<i>Correct.</i>

50:49.379 --> 50:51.006
I'm Gesicht from Europol.

50:51.715 --> 50:53.592
I'd like to ask you some questions.

50:54.634 --> 50:56.720
How is life in this prison?

50:59.264 --> 51:00.140
<i>Not bad.</i>

51:01.808 --> 51:03.351
Let's stop with the farce.

51:03.852 --> 51:06.271
- This isn't a real interview.
- Huh?

51:06.354 --> 51:08.315
There are many layers of security,

51:08.815 --> 51:11.318
so you can censor any comments
you find inconvenient.

51:11.401 --> 51:12.903
What are you talking about?

51:13.403 --> 51:15.030
Stop playing games!

51:15.655 --> 51:17.574
He is an extremely important witness!

51:18.075 --> 51:19.993
I will meet him in person.

51:20.077 --> 51:21.161
Hey, you!

51:21.244 --> 51:22.204
Wait!

51:22.704 --> 51:24.956
The president granted you
a special interview,

51:25.457 --> 51:28.210
but your actions
clearly violate international law--

51:28.293 --> 51:29.127
- Halt!
- Halt!

51:30.921 --> 51:33.965
I don't care about any relationship
between you and Europol.

51:34.049 --> 51:35.842
None of that matters!

51:35.926 --> 51:38.970
Right now, the whole world is in danger!

51:47.062 --> 51:48.772
So you're a robot.

51:49.272 --> 51:51.316
How extremely well-made.

51:51.858 --> 51:53.610
You look just like a human.

51:54.444 --> 51:57.697
I hope you're not as stupid
as humans though.

51:58.824 --> 51:59.950
Are you the mastermind

52:00.033 --> 52:03.078
behind the recent serial destruction
of advanced robots?

52:03.787 --> 52:06.331
I spoke too soon. Stupid indeed.

52:07.582 --> 52:11.753
Did you order the assassinations
of the Bora Inquiry Commission members?

52:12.671 --> 52:15.132
They are all liars.

52:15.757 --> 52:17.509
They reduced my country

52:18.468 --> 52:21.763
to a barren desert.

52:22.806 --> 52:27.269
They needed us to remain have-nots.

52:27.811 --> 52:32.691
They took everything from us,
including our glorious robot civilization.

52:33.316 --> 52:37.279
Because of their damn machines
and filthy artificial intelligence,

52:37.362 --> 52:40.157
my country was turned to ashes.

52:40.949 --> 52:44.870
Out of that resentment,
you created a robot of mass destruction.

52:45.954 --> 52:47.372
You created a monster.

52:49.374 --> 52:52.586
I created a monster?

52:53.753 --> 52:56.590
We didn't create it. It was born.

52:57.883 --> 53:03.096
He's the most capable and untarnished
of robots. One beloved by God.

53:03.180 --> 53:06.725
"Untarnished"? "Beloved by God"?

53:07.767 --> 53:10.312
A robot that repeatedly
kills and destroys?

53:10.395 --> 53:13.773
You're wrong. He was reborn.

53:14.357 --> 53:15.567
Reborn?

53:16.568 --> 53:19.321
With a stronger, more powerful body.

53:19.863 --> 53:22.365
A body that was more suited

53:22.449 --> 53:25.202
to the robotic hatred
that had spawned inside his AI.

53:25.827 --> 53:28.246
Robotic hatred.

53:30.123 --> 53:31.958
This field of flowers.

53:36.504 --> 53:38.256
This is Pluto.

53:39.925 --> 53:40.842
Pluto.

53:41.718 --> 53:42.552
Who is he?

53:43.136 --> 53:47.557
Who is Pluto? Tell me what he is!

53:48.141 --> 53:50.769
I'm sure you already know.

53:50.852 --> 53:51.728
What?

53:58.443 --> 53:59.986
He bit through his tongue!

54:00.070 --> 54:01.321
I need help!

54:01.404 --> 54:02.239
What the hell?

54:02.739 --> 54:04.241
What have you done?

54:04.324 --> 54:05.450
Call a medic!

54:05.533 --> 54:06.868
Get him out of here!

54:13.959 --> 54:17.379
"I'm sure you already know"?

54:22.175 --> 54:25.887
<i>What? Darius XIV attempted suicide?</i>

54:25.971 --> 54:28.306
Yes. But they managed to save his life.

54:29.516 --> 54:31.726
<i>You're going to get us in hot water again.</i>

54:31.810 --> 54:34.771
I'm sorry, sir.
I'm ready to take responsibility.

54:36.022 --> 54:37.691
<i>In any case, return immediately!</i>

54:41.236 --> 54:42.612
Epsilon.

54:45.115 --> 54:48.827
I couldn't reach you, so I looked up
your location and flew here.

54:52.914 --> 54:54.499
Hercules left this behind.

54:56.960 --> 54:59.754
But that's not all he left.

55:00.547 --> 55:02.132
I'd like to show you something.

55:02.632 --> 55:03.466
Huh?

55:04.050 --> 55:06.845
A great deal
of electromagnetic waves were emitted

55:07.345 --> 55:08.847
while Hercules was fighting.

55:09.806 --> 55:14.686
My analysis shows that most of them
fall into the genre of hatred.

55:16.521 --> 55:19.566
But there was a flash
of something entirely different.

55:22.152 --> 55:22.986
This is it.

55:23.486 --> 55:24.904
I'll transfer it to you now.

55:28.867 --> 55:30.493
What is this image?

55:37.792 --> 55:40.420
This couldn't possibly be.

55:43.673 --> 55:44.674
<i>Pluto?</i>

58:11.196 --> 58:14.824
Subtitle translation by: Astrid Oliver
